---Represents a Google Tag Manager Tag.
---@class gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Tag
---@field parentFolderId? string Parent folder id.
---@field firingTriggerId? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.StringList Firing trigger IDs. A tag will fire when any of the listed triggers are true and all of its blockingTriggerIds (if any specified) are false.
---@field liveOnly? boolean If set to true, this tag will only fire in the live environment (e.g. not in preview or debug mode).
---@field name? string Tag display name.
---@field paused? boolean True if the tag is paused.
---@field scheduleEndMs? string The end timestamp in milliseconds to schedule a tag.
---@field blockingTriggerId? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.StringList Blocking trigger IDs. If any of the listed triggers evaluate to true, the tag will not fire.
---@field fingerprint? string The fingerprint of the GTM Tag as computed at storage time. This value is recomputed whenever the tag is modified.
---@field type? string GTM Tag Type.
---@field notes? string User notes on how to apply this tag in the container.
---@field priority? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter User defined numeric priority of the tag. Tags are fired asynchronously in order of priority. Tags with higher numeric value fire first. A tag's priority can be a positive or negative value. The default value is 0.
---@field containerId? string GTM Container ID.
---@field tagId? string The Tag ID uniquely identifies the GTM Tag.
---@field parameter? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.ParameterList The tag's parameters.
---@field scheduleStartMs? string The start timestamp in milliseconds to schedule a tag.
---@field accountId? string GTM Account ID.
---@field tagFiringOption? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TagTagFiringOptionEnum|string Option to fire this tag.
---@field setupTag? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.SetupTagList The list of setup tags. Currently we only allow one.
---@field teardownTag? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TeardownTagList The list of teardown tags. Currently we only allow one.

---@alias gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TagList gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Tag[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TagTagFiringOptionEnum "unlimited"|"oncePerEvent"|"oncePerLoad"

---@class gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TeardownTag
---@field tagName? string The name of the teardown tag.
---@field stopTeardownOnFailure? boolean If true, fire the teardown tag if and only if the main tag fires successfully. If false, fire the teardown tag regardless of main tag firing status.

---@alias gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TeardownTagList gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TeardownTag[]

---Represents a Google Tag Manager Trigger
---@class gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Trigger
---@field parameter? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.ParameterList Additional parameters.
---@field accountId? string GTM Account ID.
---@field triggerId? string The Trigger ID uniquely identifies the GTM Trigger.
---@field autoEventFilter? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.ConditionList Used in the case of auto event tracking.
---@field uniqueTriggerId? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Globally unique id of the trigger that auto-generates this (a Form Submit, Link Click or Timer listener) if any. Used to make incompatible auto-events work together with trigger filtering based on trigger ids. This value is populated during output generation since the tags implied by triggers don't exist until then. Only valid for Form Submit, Link Click and Timer triggers.
---@field eventName? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Name of the GTM event that is fired. Only valid for Timer triggers.
---@field visibilitySelector? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A visibility trigger CSS selector (i.e. "#id"). Only valid for AMP Visibility trigger.
---@field continuousTimeMinMilliseconds? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A visibility trigger minimum continuous visible time (in milliseconds). Only valid for AMP Visibility trigger.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TriggerTypeEnum|string Defines the data layer event that causes this trigger.
---@field visiblePercentageMax? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A visibility trigger maximum percent visibility. Only valid for AMP Visibility trigger.
---@field selector? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A click trigger CSS selector (i.e. "a", "button" etc.). Only valid for AMP Click trigger.
---@field containerId? string GTM Container ID.
---@field horizontalScrollPercentageList? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter List of integer percentage values for scroll triggers. The trigger will fire when each percentage is reached when the view is scrolled horizontally. Only valid for AMP scroll triggers.
---@field fingerprint? string The fingerprint of the GTM Trigger as computed at storage time. This value is recomputed whenever the trigger is modified.
---@field name? string Trigger display name.
---@field visiblePercentageMin? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A visibility trigger minimum percent visibility. Only valid for AMP Visibility trigger.
---@field interval? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Time between triggering recurring Timer Events (in milliseconds). Only valid for Timer triggers.
---@field checkValidation? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Whether or not we should only fire tags if the form submit or link click event is not cancelled by some other event handler (e.g. because of validation). Only valid for Form Submission and Link Click triggers.
---@field totalTimeMinMilliseconds? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter A visibility trigger minimum total visible time (in milliseconds). Only valid for AMP Visibility trigger.
---@field parentFolderId? string Parent folder id.
---@field verticalScrollPercentageList? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter List of integer percentage values for scroll triggers. The trigger will fire when each percentage is reached when the view is scrolled vertically. Only valid for AMP scroll triggers.
---@field waitForTagsTimeout? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter How long to wait (in milliseconds) for tags to fire when 'waits_for_tags' above evaluates to true. Only valid for Form Submission and Link Click triggers.
---@field customEventFilter? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.ConditionList Used in the case of custom event, which is fired iff all Conditions are true.
---@field limit? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Limit of the number of GTM events this Timer Trigger will fire. If no limit is set, we will continue to fire GTM events until the user leaves the page. Only valid for Timer triggers.
---@field maxTimerLengthSeconds? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Max time to fire Timer Events (in seconds). Only valid for AMP Timer trigger.
---@field waitForTags? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Whether or not we should delay the form submissions or link opening until all of the tags have fired (by preventing the default action and later simulating the default action). Only valid for Form Submission and Link Click triggers.
---@field filter? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.ConditionList The trigger will only fire iff all Conditions are true.
---@field intervalSeconds? gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Parameter Time between Timer Events to fire (in seconds). Only valid for AMP Timer trigger.

---@alias gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TriggerList gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.Trigger[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.tagmanager_v1.TriggerTypeEnum "pageview"|"domReady"|"windowLoaded"|"customEvent"|"triggerGroup"|"always"|"formSubmission"|"click"|"linkClick"|"jsError"|"historyChange"|"timer"|"ampClick"|"ampTimer"|"ampScroll"|"ampVisibility"|"youTubeVideo"|"scrollDepth"|"elementVisibility"

